                  %div
                    %p
                      %a{:href => "/nlab/edit/string+theory+-+contents"} Edit this sidebar
          %h1#contents Contents
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#idea"} Idea
              %li
                %a{:href => "#related_concepts"} Related concepts
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The
            %em AGT correspondence
            (
            %a{:href => "#AGT09"}> AGT 09
            ) is a relation between
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                the
                = succeed "-" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/instanton"} instanton
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/partition+function"} partition function
                of
                = succeed "-" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi SU
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mn 2
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mrow
                            %mi n
                            %mo +
                            %mn 3
                            %mi g
                            %mo −
                            %mn 3
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} SU(2)^{n+3g-3}
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/N%3D2+D%3D4+super+Yang-Mills+theory"} N=2 D=4 super Yang-Mills theory
                (Nekrasov’s partition function, e.g.
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "#Szabo15"} Szabo 15 (2.1)
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+blocks"} conformal blocks
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Liouville+theory"} Liouville theory
                on an
                = succeed "-punctured" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+surface"} Riemann surface
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi C
                        %mrow
                          %mi g
                          %mo ,
                          %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{g,n}
                of
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/genus"} genus
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} g
          %p
            Here the idea is that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi C
                    %mrow
                      %mi g
                      %mo ,
                      %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C_{g,n}
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Yang-Mills+theory"} super Yang-Mills theory
            obtained by
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kaluza-Klein+mechanism"} compactifying
            the worldvolume
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/6d+%282%2C0%29-supersymmetric+QFT"} 6d (2,0)-supersymmetric QFT
            of two
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-branes"} M5-branes
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/N%3D2+D%3D4+super+Yang-Mills+theory"} N=2 D=4 super Yang-Mills theory
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "N%3D2+D%3D4+super+Yang-Mills+theory#ConstructionByCompactificationOf5Branes"} Construction by compactification
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/class+S"} class S
          %p
            In particular, the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/N%3D2+D%3D4+super+Yang-Mills+theory"} N=2 D=4 super Yang-Mills theory
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quiver+gauge+theory"} quiver gauge theory
            and the correspondence matches the shape of its
            = succeed "-diagram" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quiver"} quiver
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/genus+of+a+surface"} genus
            and punctures of the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann+surface"} Riemann surface
          %center
            %img{:src => "https://ncatlab.org/nlab/files/AGTQuiver.jpg", :width => "400"}/
          %p
            More generally, this construction yields something like a decomposition of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/6d+%282%2C0%29-superconformal+QFT"} 6d (2,0)-superconformal QFT
            into a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2d+SCFT"} 2d SCFT
            “with values in
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Yang-Mills+theory"} 4d SYM field theory
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Tachikawa10"} Tachikawa 10, slide 25 (33 of 54)
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2d+SCFT"} 2d SCFT
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2d+TQFT"} 2d TQFT
            (
            %a{:href => "#GPRR10"}> GPRR 10
            ). In this picture of “4d-SYM field theory-valued
            = succeed "\u201D" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2d+SCFT"} 2d SCFT
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+structure"} complex structure
                in 2d is the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coupling+constants"} coupling constants
                and
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/theta+angles"} theta angles
                etc in the 4d
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+Yang-Mills+theory"} super Yang-Mills theory
            %li
              %p
                the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/mapping+class+group"} mapping class group
                (large
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/conformal+transformations"} conformal transformations
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/S-duality"} S-duality
                of the 4d theory.
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-brane+elliptic+genus"} M5-brane elliptic genus
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality+in+physics"}> duality in physics
                ,
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/duality+in+string+theory"} duality in string theory
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Nekrasov+function"} Nekrasov function
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/McKay+correspondence"} McKay correspondence
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/3d-3d+correspondence"} 3d-3d correspondence
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/knots-quivers+correspondence"} knots-quivers correspondence
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/class+S"} class S
          %p
            Wrapping the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-brane"} M5-brane
            on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/3-manifold"} 3-manifold
            instead yields:
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/3d-3d+correspondence"} 3d-3d correspondence
          %h2#references References
          %p
            A
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2d+SCFT"} 2d SCFT
            argued to describe the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/KK-compactification"} KK-compactification
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/M5-brane"} M5-brane
            on a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/4-manifold"} 4-manifold
            (specifically: a
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+surface"} complex surface
          %ul
            %li
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Juan+Maldacena"}> Juan Maldacena
              ,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrew+Strominger"} Andrew Strominger
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Edward+Witten"} Edward Witten
              = succeed "," do
                %em Black Hole Entropy in M-Theory
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/hep-th/9711053"} arXiv:hep-th/9711053
          %p The origin of the AGT correspondence is:
          %ul
            %li#Gaiotto09
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Davide+Gaiotto"}> Davide Gaiotto
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi N
                          %mo =
                          %mn 2
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N=2
                    dualities
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0904.2715"} arXiv:0904.2715
            %li#AGT09
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Luis+Alday"}> Luis Alday
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Davide+Gaiotto"} Davide Gaiotto
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yuji+Tachikawa"} Yuji Tachikawa
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Liouville Correlation Functions from Four-dimensional Gauge Theories
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0906.3219"} arXiv:0906.3219
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Davide+Gaiotto"}> Davide Gaiotto
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Gregory+Moore"} Gregory Moore
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrew+Neitzke"} Andrew Neitzke
                %em
                  Wall-crossing, Hitchin systems, and the WKB approximation, Advances in Mathematics
                  %strong 234
                  (2013) 239–403 (
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0907.3987"} arXiv:0907.3987
                  = succeed ")" do
                    %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1016/j.aim.2012.09.027"} doi
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/2d+TQFT"} 2d TQFT
            obtained from this by forming the 4d index is discussed in
          %ul
            %li#GPRR10
              Abhijit Gadde, Elli Pomoni,
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Leonardo+Rastelli"} Leonardo Rastelli
              = succeed "," do
                %em S-duality and 2d Topological QFT
              = succeed ")" do
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/0910.2225"} arXiv:0910.2225
          %p
            Relation of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/AGT-correspondence"} AGT-correspondence
            to the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/D%3D6+N%3D%282%2C0%29+SCFT"} D=6 N=(2,0) SCFT
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Benjamin Assel,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sakura+Schafer-Nameki"} Sakura Schafer-Nameki
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    M5-branes on
                    = succeed ":" do
                      %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                        %semantics
                          %mrow
                            %msup
                              %mi S
                              %mn 2
                            %mo ×
                            %msub
                              %mi M
                              %mn 4
                          %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S^2 \times M_4
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1604.03606"} arxiv:1604.03606
              %p
                (relating to the
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/moduli+space+of+monopoles"} moduli space of monopoles
          %p
            and to the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/3d-3d+correspondence"} 3d-3d correspondence
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Clay+Cordova"}> Clay Cordova
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Daniel+Jafferis"} Daniel Jafferis
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Toda Theory From Six Dimensions
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1605.03997"} arxiv:1605.03997
            %li
              %p
                Sam van Leuven, Gerben Oling,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Generalized Toda Theory from Six Dimensions and the Conifold
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1708.07840"} arxiv:1708.07840
          %p Brief surveys include
          %ul
            %li#Tachikawa10
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Yuji+Tachikawa"}> Yuji Tachikawa
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em M5-branes, 4d gauge theory and 2d CFT
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://member.ipmu.jp/yuji.tachikawa/transp/4d-2d-caltech.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                Abhijit Gadde,
                %em
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi 𝒩
                        %mo =
                        %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{N}= 2
                  Dualities and 2d TQFT
                2012 (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/files/Gadde2dTQFT.pdf", :title => "pdf"}> pdf
                )
            %li
              %p
                Nikolay Bovev,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em New SCFTs from wrapped branes
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://ipht.cea.fr/Meetings/Itzykson2013/Talks/bobev-Itzykson-july2013.pdf"} pdf
            %li
              %p
                Giulio Bonelli,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Variations on AGT Correspondence
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://indico.cern.ch/event/217384/attachments/348854/486363/Bonelli.pdf"} pdf
            %li#Taki16
              %p
                Masato Taki,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em String Theory as an Attempt of PolyMathematics
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://indico2.riken.jp/event/2215/attachments/4106/4775/Taki_invited.pdf"} pdf
          %p More detailed review is in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                Rober Rodger,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A pedagogical introduction to the AGT conjecture
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://testweb.science.uu.nl/ITF/teaching/2013/R.J.Rodger.pdf"} pdf
            %li#Szabo15
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Richard+Szabo"}> Richard Szabo
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi N
                          %mo =
                          %mn 2
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} N=2
                    gauge theories, instanton moduli spaces and geometric representation theory
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1507.00685"} arXiv:1507.00685
            %li
              %p
                Bruno Le Floch,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em A slow review of the AGT correspondence
                %strong 55
                (2022) 353002 (
                %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1088/1751-8121/ac5945"} doi
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2006.14025"} arXiv:2006.14025
          %p See also
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Alexander+Belavin"}> Alexander Belavin
                , M. A. Bershtein, B. L. Feigin, A. V. Litvinov, G. M. Tarnopolsky,
                %em Instanton moduli spaces and bases in coset conformal field theory
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1111.2803"}> arxiv/1111.2803
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Volker+Schomerus"}> Volker Schomerus
                , Paulina Suchanek,
                %em Liouville’s imaginary shadow
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1210.1856"}> arxiv/1210.1856
                )
            %li
              %p
                A.Mironov, A.Morozov,
                %em The power of Nekrasov functions
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0908.2190"}> arxiv/0908.2190
                )
            %li
              %p
                D. Galakhov, A. Mironov, A. Morozov,
                %em S-duality as a beta-deformed Fourier transform
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1205.4998"}> arxiv/1205.4998
                )
            %li
              %p
                A. Mironov,
                %em Spectral duality in integrable systems from AGT conjecture
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1204.0913"}> arxiv/1204.0913
                )
            %li
              %p
                A. Belavin, V. Belavin,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    AGT conjecture and integrable structure of conformal field theory for
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi c
                          %mo =
                          %mn 1
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c=1
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1102.0343"} arxiv/1102.0343
            %li
              %p
                A. Belavin, V. Belavin, M. Bershtein,
                %em Instantons and 2d Superconformal field theory
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1106.4001"}> arxiv/1106.4001
                )
            %li
              %p
                Kazunobu Maruyoshi,
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Quantum integrable systems, matrix models, and AGT correspondence
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://db.ipmu.jp/seminar/sysimg/seminar/428.pdf"} slides pdf
            %li
              %p
                Giulio Bonelli, Alessandro Tanzini,
                %em Hitchin systems, N=2 gauge theories and W-gravity
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/0909.4031"}> arxiv/0909.4031
                )
            %li
              %p
                Giulio Bonelli, Kazunobu Maruyoshi, Alessandro Tanzini,
                %em Quantum Hitchin systems via beta-deformed matrix models
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1104.4016"}> arxiv/1104.4016
                )
            %li#ChacaltanaDistler10
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Oscar+Chacaltana"}> Oscar Chacaltana
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jacques+Distler"} Jacques Distler
                = succeed "," do
                  %em Tinkertoys for Gaiotto Duality
                = succeed ")" do
                  %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/arXiv:1008.5203"} arXiv:1008.5203
            %li
              %p
                Satoshi Nawata,
                %em Givental J-functions, Quantum integrable systems, AGT relation with surface operator
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1408.4132"}> arXiv/1408.4132
                )
          %p
            The AGT correspondence is treated with the help of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Riemann-Hilbert+problem"} Riemann-Hilbert problem
            in
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                G. Vartanov,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/J%C3%B6rg+Teschner"} Jörg Teschner
                %em Supersymmetric gauge theories, quantization of moduli spaces of flat connections, and conformal field theory
                (
                %a{:href => "http://arxiv.org/abs/1302.3778"}> arxiv/1302.3778
                )
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrei+Mironov"}> Andrei Mironov
                , A. Morozov,
                %em Superintegrability as the hidden origin of Nekrasov calculus
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2207.08242"}> arXiv:2207.08242
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p Proof of the AGT conjecture in special cases:
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrei+Mironov"}> Andrei Mironov
                ,
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Andrey+Morozov"} Andrey Morozov
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sh.+Shakirov"} Sh. Shakirov
                = succeed "," do
                  %em
                    A direct proof of AGT conjecture at
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi β
                          %mo =
                          %mn 1
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta = 1
                = succeed "," do
                  %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/1012.3137"} arXiv:1012.3137
                = succeed "&rbrack;" do
                  %a{:href => "https://doi.org/10.1007/JHEP02(2011)067"} doi:10.1007/JHEP02(2011)067
            %li
              %p
                Qing-Jie Yuan, Shao-Ping Hu, Zi-Hao Huang, Kilar Zhang,
                %em
                  A proof of An AGT conjecture at
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi β
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta = 1
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2305.11839"}> arXiv:2305.11839
                \&amp;rbrack;
            %li
              %p
                Qian Shen, Zi-Hao Huang, Shao-Ping Hu, Qing-Jie Yuan, Kilar Zhang,
                %em
                  Proof of 5D
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi A
                          %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A_n
                  AGT conjecture at
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi β
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \beta=1
                \&amp;lbrack;
                %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2405.13676"}> arXiv:2405.13676
                \&amp;rbrack;
          %p See also:
          %ul
            %li
              Leszek Hadasz, Błażej Ruba,
              %em
                Decomposition of
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mover
                          %mi sl
                          %mo ^
                        %mrow
                          %mn 2
                          %mo ,
                          %mi k
                      %mo ⊗
                      %msub
                        %mover
                          %mi sl
                          %mo ^
                        %mrow
                          %mn 2
                          %mo ,
                          %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \widehat{sl}_{2,k} \otimes \widehat{sl}_{2,1}
                highest weight representations for generic level
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
                and equivalence between two dimensional CFT models
              \&amp;lbrack;
              %a{:href => "https://arxiv.org/abs/2312.14695"}> arXiv:2312.14695
              \&amp;rbrack;
          .property
            category:
            %a.category_link{:href => "/nlab/all_pages/physics"} physics
